  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "\tThat's right, folks\u2014beloved giraffe Frankenfurt has been returned
    to her enclosure as of this morning, following a police chase that can only be
    described as a sight for the ages. \n\tOne week ago, on November 9th, the Woodland
    Park Zoo issued an official statement to say that a giraffe had escaped and that
    any and all tips to its whereabouts would be greatly appreciated. Though this
    led to several hoaxes throughout the week, including a large blow-up dinosaur
    which blocked traffic downtown for the better part of an hour, zoo officials
    finally found the animal in Discovery Park, over three miles away from the zoo
    itself. How a giraffe crossed Ballard Bridge unhindered, Seattle may never know.\n\tFor
    those who didn't get a chance to spot her in the wild, the Woodland Park Zoo
    is open 9am-6pm from Tuesday-Saturday. When asked for comment, zoo officials
    said, \"Come to the zoo! We have Frankenfurt plushies!\"\n\tThese statements
    do not reflect the views or opinions of the Seattle Times.\n\n\xA9 Seattle Times,
    2002\nAuthor Sam Muffie"
